Why this file exists
--------------------

LICENSE is the verbatim text of the AGPL, and the only copyright line inside it belongs
to the Free Software Foundation, for the licence document itself. It says nothing about
who owns this software. Before the relicense, the MIT LICENSE carried that notice; the
swap would otherwise have dropped the repository's only assertion of authorship.

AGPL section 5(a) requires a modified version to carry prominent notices of its
modification, and section 14 makes "version 3 only" versus "version 3 or later" a
statement the copyright holder has to actually make somewhere. This file is where both
live. The project is AGPL-3.0-**only**: no proxy is designated under section 14 to
approve later versions on the copyright holder's behalf.

If you fork this and modify it, add your own line below rather than replacing the one
above. Copyright accumulates; it does not transfer by editing a file.

Contributors keep copyright in what they write, and license it to everyone under the
AGPL by contributing — there is no contributor licence agreement and no copyright
assignment. `CONTRIBUTORS.md` credits the people who built this.

